      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0004-l0000",
      "p0001-n0004-l0001",
      "p0001-n0004-l0002",
      "p0001-n0004-l0003",
      "p0001-n0004-l0004",
      "p0001-n0004-l0005",
      "p0001-n0004-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In Task2: First, we use a linear programming model to quantitatively analyze, and in the case of  limited optimization costs, we transform the problem into maximizing the system maturity index. Then, we use system dynamics to simulate and obtain the index values corresponding to different maturity levels for qualitative analysis, verifying the validity of the model by comparing the difference between the simulation results and the evaluation model of task 1. Finally, we com- bine the two methods, and based on the differences between the fourth and fifth levels of maturity, we give suggestions that ICM companies need to invest in teamwork and technical management."
  },
